  <keyword>dataStoreWrite</keyword>
  <keyword_alias>block:dataStoreWrite</keyword_alias>
  <short_description>Writes its input to the named data store.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>Block type: dataStoreWrite</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>input ports</param_name>
      <param_description>1 input port(s) declared.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>output ports</param_name>
      <param_description>No output ports (this block has none).</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Writes its input to the named data store.</p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Module</td><td><code>nflow_blocks</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Library</td><td>Utility</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Type</td><td><code>dataStoreWrite</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Label</td><td>Data Store Write</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><img src="../../../../libraries/utility/exports/dataStoreWrite.svg" align="middle"/></p>
    <p><b>Description</b></p>
    <p>Writes the input value to the named memory <code>DataStoreName</code> declared by a <code>dataStoreMemory</code> block (a matching entry is created if none exists). The write happens in the UPDATE phase, so a <code>dataStoreRead</code> of the same name observes it on the next step. One input, no output. Native only; scalar.</p>
    <p><b>Ports</b></p>
    <p><b>Input(s)</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Port</th><th>Role</th><th>Side</th><th>Position</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Port_1</td><td>Numeric signal read by the block.</td><td>left</td><td>x=0, y=30</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>This block has no output ports.</p>
    <p><b>Parameters</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Default value</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>DataStoreName</code></td><td>A</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Block Characteristics</b></p>
    <table border="1">
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Block type</td><td>dataStoreWrite</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Family</td><td>Utility</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Rendered size</td><td>70 x 60</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Phases</td><td>INIT, UPDATE</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Internal state or history</td><td>yes</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Signal data type</td><td>double numeric values</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p><b>Algorithms</b></p>
    <ul>
      <li>UPDATE: store[DataStoreName] = u.</li>
    </ul>
    <p><b>Extended Capabilities</b></p>
    <p>Native runtime only (this block is not code-generated).</p>
    <p>Code generation: supported for C and Rust.</p>
    <p><b>Implementation Sources</b></p>
